  "details": "When I enabled AFK Detection on desktop client, I pressed the End key to go AFK. I realized I was going to be out longer than expected, so I logged out while in AFK state.\n\nLater, I logged in on SteamVR client, and my avatar was still in an AFK state with my headset on, and SteamVR dashboard closed.\n\nTurning off AFK Detection in the Action Menu fixed the issue, but I wanted to enable detection. When I turned it back on, my avatar went immediately into AFK state. \n\nRelaunching VRChat doesn't seem to fix the issue at all.",
